The OpenJDK in the executables Nabu produces
--------------------------------------------

Nabu does not contain the Java class library. The LLVM backend (and the nabu-native-image command) reads the JDK
that runs the compiler and compiles the bytecode of the classes a program can reach, the classes of java.base and
other JDK modules among them, into the executable. The OpenJDK is licensed under the GNU General Public License,
version 2, with the Classpath Exception (https://openjdk.org/legal/gplv2+ce.html). For the executables that means:

  * An executable contains OpenJDK code, compiled from the class files of the JDK it was built with. The Classpath
    Exception lets you link that code with your own, independent code and distribute the result under terms of your
    choice, provided that you meet the terms of the license of each linked module.

  * Nabu changes some of the OpenJDK code it compiles: it replaces the bodies of some methods, redirects some calls
    (String.format inside the JDK, for example) and leaves out code that cannot run in a native executable. The
    replacement code is in compiler/src/main/java/io/github/potjerodekool/nabu/compiler/backend/bytecode
    (substitutions and runtime) and in runtime/ (the C runtime). The changed OpenJDK code remains under the GNU
    General Public License, version 2, with the Classpath Exception.

  * Whoever distributes an executable therefore distributes OpenJDK code, and should include the license text
    (https://openjdk.org/legal/gplv2+ce.html) and say where the source of that code can be had: the source of the
    OpenJDK release the executable was built with is at https://openjdk.org/, and the replacements are the Nabu source
    named above.

The Java time zone database
---------------------------

The executable reads time zones from lib/tzdb.dat. Nabu copies that file from the JDK it runs on to the directory of
the executable (a lib directory next to it). It is part of the OpenJDK and falls under the same license as the
classes above; distribute it with the executable under the same terms.

Other components
----------------

The libraries Nabu uses and links, and their licenses, are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md; the texts of the licenses
are in the directory licenses/.

What is Nabu's own
------------------

The compiler, the backends, the plugins, the C runtime in runtime/ and the substitution classes are written for
Nabu and are under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The substitution classes only describe what replaces the body
of a JDK method; they are not part of the OpenJDK.
